<%# The beta strip, above the bar on every account page: what this account is,
    what comes back to a respondent through it, and that it is still being
    built.

    Rendered from you/_bar rather than from the four pages, because what it
    says is true of the account as a whole rather than of the dashboard — a
    respondent reaches the wallet and the Verto pages from a card without
    passing the dashboard again, and "we're just getting started" is the
    answer to whatever they find half-finished there. The bar is the one
    thing all four pages share, so riding with it is what keeps the strip
    from going missing on the page that needs it.

    Signed out too: the signed-out page is still the account, and someone
    deciding whether to give an email address at the end of a Verto is
    exactly who the welcome is addressed to.

    Not dismissible on purpose — there is no state to hang a dismissal on for
    a signed-out reader, and a notice that disappears on first sight is one
    the next visit cannot answer a question with. It comes down when the
    account is no longer a beta. %>
<div class="you-beta">
  <div class="you-beta-inner">
    <span class="you-beta-tag"><%= t("you.beta_tag") %></span>
    <p class="you-beta-text"><%= t("you.beta_note") %></p>
  </div>
</div>
